# API Routes Module Rules

## Purpose
Next.js API routes and webhook handlers. Handles HTTP requests, webhooks (Stripe, BetterAuth), and server-side business logic.

## Entry Points
- `src/app/api/**/route.ts` - API route handlers
- `src/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts` - BetterAuth catch-all route
- `src/app/api/payments/webhook/route.ts` - Stripe webhook handler
- `src/app/api/template/route.ts` - Template API route

## Allowed Imports
- `@/lib/*` - Core utilities (db, auth, ratelimiter, redis)
- `@/utils/*` - Helper functions
- `next/server` - NextRequest, NextResponse
- Drizzle ORM for database operations
- Stripe SDK for payment processing
- BetterAuth for authentication

## Forbidden Imports
- `@/components/*` - No React components in API routes
- `@/app/**` - No importing from other app routes
- Client-side libraries (React, React DOM)

## Coding Conventions

### Route Handler Structure
```typescript
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { db } from "@/lib/db";

export async function GET(req: NextRequest) {
  // Handler logic
  return NextResponse.json({ data });
}

export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  // Handler logic
  return NextResponse.json({ data });
}
```

### Rate Limiting
- Always use rate limiting for public endpoints
- Import `ratelimit` from `@/lib/ratelimiter`
- Check rate limit before processing requests

### Authentication
- Use BetterAuth for session validation
- Import `auth` from `@/lib/auth`
- Check authentication for protected endpoints

### Database Operations
- Use Drizzle ORM for all database queries
- Import `db` from `@/lib/db` and call `db()` to get instance
- Use type-safe queries with schema imports

### Error Handling
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes
- Use NextResponse.json() for JSON responses
- Handle errors gracefully with try-catch blocks

### Webhook Security
- Verify webhook signatures (Stripe, BetterAuth)
- Use environment variables for webhook secrets
- Validate request payloads

### Request Validation
- Validate input data using Zod schemas
- Check required environment variables
- Sanitize user input

## AI Hints
- Always implement rate limiting for public endpoints
- Use Drizzle ORM for type-safe database queries
- Follow RESTful conventions for route naming
- Return proper HTTP status codes
- Keep route handlers focused and single-purpose
- Use async/await for all async operations
